{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027659-arete-5-should-i-stay-or-should-i-go","id":1027659,"title":"Arete 5: Should i stay or Should i Go?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-06T08:03:42-08:00","id":1027659,"title":"Arete 5: Should i stay or Should i Go?","content":"couple of friends told me many times that, once a mage achieves arete 5, reality basically kicks him out and its forced to live in exile within the umbra/far reaches etc...<br /> <br /> how true is this? can a mage with arete 5 or higher stay in earth with out breaking it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:29:41-08:00","id":1027683,"title":"","content":"There is an Arete 7 Syndic who seems to be running a casino and visiting a hunting lodge in the woods just fine. His write up mentions nothing about him needing to stay in one place; an Arete 8 Nephandus from <i>Book of Chantries</i> is described as having a different form (that of an old man) on Earth. Some high Arete Mages need to stay in the Umbra or a Sanctum because accumulated Paradox (often from longevity/immortality rotes) will destroy them if they walk around Earth (or so they think..), but this doesn't have to happen to every high Arete Mage. The Aswadim are described as helping out some Nephandi from time to time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-07-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:31:24-08:00","id":1027684,"title":"","content":"Your friends are wrong. It is Paradox, not Arete, that drives mages off of Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:37:37-08:00","id":1027692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1027659-arete-5-should-i-stay-or-should-i-go?p=1027684#post1027684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your friends are wrong. It is Paradox, not Arete, that drives mages off of Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure this is right. I think the strength/threat of backlash just gets too intense?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:12:01-08:00","id":1027737,"title":"","content":"More that high Arete Mages are more likely to accrue Paradox, and able to do so in greater amounts.<br /> <br /> Also, as stated, Permadox of every sorts plays a role.<br /> <br /> But it is all statistics. Arete or Sphere level don't make for instant kick from reality, nor instant severity in Paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:15:56-08:00","id":1027739,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea of Mages not being able to remain in the world after Arete 5 is not just arbitrary, it's unfair to player characters. You spend an entire chronicle slowly building your magickal power, going beyond the level of even a Master. If you're a technomancer (at least according to M20), you can finally start abandoning Instruments (and I seem to recall this being true of all Mages pre-M20). It's unreasonable to then tell that player &quot;you can no longer operate in the world, sucks to be you&quot;.<br /> <br /> In reality, it's Permanent Paradox, not Arete, that limits a Mage's ability to remain in the material world. Maybe they've modified themselves in obviously supernatural ways (animal features, 6+ dot Attributes, extensive cybernetic augmentation), or maybe they've prolonged their life to the point where their continued existence is a crime against the Consensus. Whatever the case, it's not impossible for a Mage like this to take a walk down the street in broad daylight. They just dare not use Vulgar magick in any capacity, since they garner dangerous levels of Paradox with each shot.<br /> <br /> A relatively young Archmage, however, who hasn't overtly altered their pattern, doesn't have to worry about that. If it seems unlikely that a person could achieve archmastery within a normal human lifetime, remember that Adventurers (Player Characters) tend to progress faster than NPCs, because they seek challenge (and thus garner more Experience). Any PC worth their salt will at least shoot for Mastery, if not higher, for any number of reasons. <i>Masters of the Art</i> is a book built around the assumption that archmasters could either be aloof elders living in Sancta or Horizon realms, or Mages whose lifestyles are largely unchanged (save that they are more powerful). That book has sections devoted to roleplaying characters that try to interact with the mundane world, in light of their enhanced Enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T16:34:23-08:00","id":1028327,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think your friends may have been confusing a Marauder's Quiet with Arete for mages in general. At some point the disconnect of the former from consensual reality causes it to spit the mage into the more forgiving Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:50:31-08:00","id":1028566,"title":"","content":"All of the above, plus it SO depends on the mage and on the combination of her Faction, Sect, amount of Resonance, Permadox, Focus and general way of going about doing reality work. <br /> <br /> An extensively modified cyborg It-X archmage who has been involved in open warfare against Reality Deviants of all stripes is going to have a hard time even walking down the street in broad daylight without some prior planning (e.g. use your pull with the Syndicate to arrange to film an appropriate movie or TV show in the area). But an It-X Time Motion manager with concealed implants who has worked extensively trying to upgrade Consensus technology over a long career might be able to live a fairly normal mundane life. Even their Resonance probably wouldn't be an issue if they kept to their normal lifestyle (attending Burning Man or a tent revival might be an issue. Flying coach, attending a business meeting or walking the floor of a factory probably wouldn't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}